  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "CI05111",
    "sub_id": "27420",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>評分標準含平時表現、期中考、期末考</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>期中考與期末考採取紙筆考試</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>The grading components include coursework, the midterm exam, and the final exam.<br />\nBoth the midterm and final exams will be administered as paper&nbsp;tests.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n",
    "course_pol": "課堂行為\n\n1. 學生應準時出席上課。如果您的上課時間，無法按時到課，請不要選課。 除非您生病或有緊急情況，否則應在上課前，要準時到達教室，並坐在位子上。如果您有某種原因必須提早下課，請提前告知我。\n2. 本課程實施點名到課率至少80%，未達標準則平時成績以零分計算並且期末考扣考。\n3. 上課時請勿講話、閱讀、睡覺或做其他非本課程相關作業，除分組進行討論外，否則應盡量減少邊際對話。\n4. 允許使用筆記型電腦或平板等載具，進行課堂記筆記，否則應將其收起。\n5. 要確保在上課時，關閉手機，如全程上課期間過度使用手機者將視為曠課。\n6. 不得戴耳機上課。\n7. 穿著整潔，不要暴露。",
    "course_pol_en": "Classroom Conduct\n\n1. Students are expected to attend class on time. If you cannot arrive punctually for this course, please do not enroll. Unless you are ill or facing an emergency, you should arrive before class begins, be seated, and ready for instruction. If you must leave early for any reason, please inform me in advance.\n2. Attendance will be taken. Students must attend at least 80% of class meetings. Those who do not meet this requirement will receive a zero for class participation and will not be allowed to take the final exam.\n3. During class, please refrain from talking, reading, sleeping, or doing work unrelated to this course. Except during group discussions, side conversations should be kept to a minimum.\n4. Laptops or tablets may be used for taking notes. Otherwise, they should be put away.\n5. Please ensure that your mobile phone is turned off during class. Excessive phone use during the entire class session will be considered an absence.\n6. Wearing earphones in class is not permitted.\n7. Students should dress neatly and avoid overly revealing clothing.",
    "course_rem": "1. 請避免使用 iLearn 2的聊天功能與授課教師聯繫重要事務。\n2. 各項聯繫請盡量使用電子郵件。\n3. 電子郵寄中請詳細闡明寄件者與信件主旨，信件內容起頭請說明寄件者姓名與班級，並學習以\"您\"稱為授課教師。",
    "course_rem_en": "1. Please avoid using the iLearn 2 chat function to communicate important matters with the instructor.\n2. For all course-related communication, please use email whenever possible.\n3. In your emails, clearly specify the sender and the subject of the message. At the beginning of the email, please state your name and class, and address the instructor respectfully using the appropriate honorific form.",
    "ais_meno": "<div>學習必須以誠信為基礎，在作業、測驗或考試中作弊或抄襲的學生或協助他人的行為，該次成績以零分計，若是累犯，將依逢甲大學學生獎懲辦法提送。\n<ul>\n\t<li>各項考試如小考、期中考、期末考時如果抄襲他人的答案則視為作弊。</li>\n\t<li>繳交作業或是各項報告時若抄襲全部或部分由他人撰寫的內容(含直接複製線上得到的內容)，則被視為作弊。</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Learning must be grounded in academic integrity. Students who cheat or plagiarize on assignments, quizzes, or exams&mdash;or assist others in doing so&mdash;will receive a zero for that task. Repeat offenders will be referred for disciplinary action in accordance with Feng Chia University&rsquo;s Student Conduct Regulations.</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<div>Cheating includes copying answers from others during quizzes, midterm exams, or final exams.</div>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<div>Plagiarism includes submitting assignments or reports that contain, in whole or in part, content written by someone else (including material directly copied from online sources).</div>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
